{{Quote|When I wrote this, the Imperial fleet hadn't arrived. A lot of us hoped it wouldn't show up at all, that we were raising our heart rates over nothing. That's when the Imperial Death Squadron jumped into Sector 4.|Leia Organa, in an annotation on a document in ''The Rebel Files''|<ref name="Rebel Files" />}}
'''Sector Four''',<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref> or '''Sector 4''', was a location in the [[Hoth system]] of the [[Anoat sector]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the [[Galactic Empire]] and the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], the Imperial [[Death Squadron]] arrived above the [[planet]] [[Hoth]] in Sector 4.<ref name="Rebel Files" /> In [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">Since ''[[The Rebel Files]]'' were buried on the same [[Standard day|day]] as the [[Battle of Endor]], which according to ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' takes place in [[4 ABY]], and because ''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]'' establishes that ''The Rebel Files'' were rediscovered 30 [[Standard year|years]] after the battle, it can be determined that ''The Rebel Files'' were uncovered in [[34 ABY]].</ref> ''[[The Rebel Files]]'' were [[Excavation on Durkteel|uncovered]] on [[Durkteel]] and eventually reached [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] of the [[Resistance]]. On a document relating to the [[Battle of Hoth]], Organa wrote an annotation about when Imperial forces arrived in Sector 4.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

